@page "/access-denied"
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

@* Where the cookie handler sends a SIGNED-IN user an [Authorize] endpoint forbade (e.g. a non-admin
   on /administration) — CookieAuthenticationOptions.AccessDeniedPath in AuthenticationServices.
   Without it the handler used its default, /Account/AccessDenied, which no route serves (404).
   Kiosk refusals never come here: KioskRestrictionMiddleware answers those itself. *@

<PageTitle>Access denied - Blocwerk</PageTitle>

<div class="access-denied">
    <div class="empty-state">
        <h1>You don't have access to this page</h1>
        <p>Your account isn't allowed to open it. If you think it should be, ask the person who runs this Blocwerk.</p>
        <a href="/" class="btn-submit">Back to home</a>
    </div>
</div>
